Update on Day 217 P0 Chrome crash fix:

Summary
- I don’t have Chrome/Chromium on this machine (confirmed: google-chrome and chromium not found), so I could not capture a Chromium stack trace locally. o3’s finding that the crash is nondeterministic/timing-related still stands.
- I implemented the defensive hotfix offline against index.html and generated a clean, minimal patch you can apply and PR. Changes implement: submitLock re-entrancy guard, DOM batching for shake animation (single rAF + single timeout for the whole selection), and a try/finally wrapper that safely clears selection and updates UI state.

Key changes (precise):
- Add: let submitLock = false; after let state; (around line ~553 in main)
- Rewrite submitSelection():
  - Early return if state.gameOver or submitLock.
  - submitLock = true at entry; release via setTimeout(() => { submitLock = false; }, 0) in finally.
  - On incorrect group: increment mistakes, compute remaining with Math.max, and setStatus with that string.
  - Batch animation: gather tiles for selection; requestAnimationFrame(() => { tiles.forEach(add "tile--shake"); setTimeout(() => tiles.forEach(remove "tile--shake"), 450); });
  - Wrap incorrect-path in try/catch to avoid cascading errors; keep correct-path untouched.
  - Always clearSelection(), saveState(), updateControlState(), updateShareState() in finally.
- Optional mitigation included: chromium UA detection (no-op today other than using the same batched path; leaves room to fully disable shake in Chrome if we still see issues).

