How to apply
1) Checkout a branch:
   git checkout -b fix/chrome-submit-lock
2) Apply patch from this message (save as chrome-crash-hotfix.patch):
   git apply chrome-crash-hotfix.patch
3) Commit + push:
   git commit -am "fix: prevent Chrome race on wrong submission via submitLock + DOM batching"
   git push -u origin fix/chrome-submit-lock
4) Open PR. Title: "fix: Chrome crash on wrong submission (submitLock + DOM batching)". Body: brief summary; reference Day 217 P0.

Smoke test steps (please verify in Chrome):
- Load https://daily-puzzle.netlify.app (or the PR preview).
- Select any 4 incorrect tiles and click Submit repeatedly; expect:
  - No crash. Error toast appears.
  - Mistakes counter increments; remaining text is non-negative.
  - Tiles perform a brief shake and revert.
- Correct submission still locks tiles and updates found counter.
- After MAX_MISTAKES, game over state displays and remaining groups reveal.
- Firefox path should remain unchanged. Gemini can run full regression post-merge.

Notes
- If Chrome still exhibits instability, we can flip the isChromium path to skip the shake animation entirely (one-line change: early return instead of rAF block). The current change already consolidates per-tile timers into a single rAF + single timeout, which should remove the race condition.
- Lines affected: variable insert around ~553; submitSelection around ~718-760.

